  "unit": 30,
  "title": "In the park",
  "description": "Name what is in a park, and talk about the small things there.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "A park is full of small nouns: swings, paths, ants. They follow the usual rules, and the plural is where most of the interest is.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "La brisa, la mariposa, la hormiga, la sombra and la hoja are feminine. El columpio, el tobogán, el paseo, el nido and el sendero are masculine. El paseo is the walk itself, and el sendero is the path through the park.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el columpio",
            "en": "the swing"
          },
          {
            "es": "la mariposa",
            "en": "the butterfly"
          },
          {
            "es": "el sendero",
            "en": "the path"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "A park full of plurals",
        "body": "The plural adds -s or -es: las mariposas, los columpios, las hormigas. Two of these words are a little different: el paseo becomes los paseos, and el tobogán becomes los toboganes, because the -án keeps its accent in the singular and drops it in the plural.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "las mariposas",
            "en": "the butterflies"
          },
          {
            "es": "los columpios",
            "en": "the swings"
          },
          {
            "es": "un paseo por el parque",
            "en": "a walk through the park"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
